@mgol Thanks for the quick response. 

> There was a recent spec change that require CSS Custom Properties values to be trimmed and it's just been implemented in Firefox 91 so far. 

Yes, so in my option, test case [css(--customProperty)](https://github.com/jquery/jquery/blob/main/test/unit/css.js#L1780) is  more appropriate to be modified  to `assert.equal( $elem.css( "--prop2" ), "val2", "Trim whitespace" );` because Travis tests has failed now and all browsers will implement the spec change eventually.
